  "body": "## What changed\n\n`probe_tormach` failed 6 of 7 on main. #579 (#570) and #583 merged two minutes apart. #583's Tormach probe goldens had been written against the probe cycle from before #570, so they still expected the old unsafe descent.\n\nThe six `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach/probe_*.nc` goldens are regenerated (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1`). No code changes.\n\nI read each diff against #570's rule:\n- **Before (stale golden):** `G0 ... Z0.9843`, a rapid straight down to 25 mm over the part, then the probe.\n- **After (main's output):** `G0 ... Z1.9685`, a rapid only to the 50 mm safe plane, then `G38.3 ... Z0.9843` as a protected positioning feed with its hit check.\n- **No rapid below the safe plane:** none of the six files has a `G0` below the safe plane (checked with a script). The metric bore is the same, with its rapid stopping at Z50 and `G38.3` to Z25.\n- **O-word numbers** (`o500N`) shift by one for the added guard.\n\n## Pinned by\n\n`probe_tormach`, all 7 tests: `face_posts_g38_2_and_sets_z_on_the_770mx`, `edge_…`, `bore_…`, `corner_…`, `boss_…`, `bore_posts_in_mm_on_a_metric_machine`.\n\n## How tested\n\n`probe_tormach` (7/7), `probe_guard` (5/5, which reads `tormach/probe_guard_moves.nc`, unchanged) and `probe_op` (12/12) pass on upstream main c81cdd52 plus this commit.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nOther app suites: no other suite reads these six goldens.\n\nThe branch is cut from upstream/main because the break only exists there. The fork is synced at v0.16.0.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #695\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
